.²1 A mark, token, sign, indication, characteristic, distinctive mark;
 {#vaDUdukUlaM kalahaMsalakzaRam#} <ls>Ku. 5. 67</ls>; {#anAramBo hi kAryARAM praTamaM#}
 {#budDilakzaRam#} <ls>Subhāṣ.</ls>; {#upakArApakArO hi lakzyaM lakzaRametayoH#}
 <ls>H. 4. 15</ls>; {#avyAkzepo BavizyantyAH kAryasidDerhi lakzaRam#} <ls>R. 10. 6</ls>, <ls n="R.">19. 47</ls>;
 {#garBalakzaRa#} <ls>Ś. 5</ls>; {#puruzalakzaRam#} ‘the sign or organ of virility’.
.²2 A symptom (of a disease).
.²3 An attribute, a quality.
.²4 A definition, accurate description; {#asADAraRaDarmo lakzaRam#}; {#nAmaDeyena#}
 {#padArTamAtrasyABiDAnamuddeSaH, tatroddizwasyAtattvavyavacCedako Darmo#}
 {#lakzaRam#} <ls>Vātsyāyana Bhāṣya 1. 1. 2</ls>.
.²5 A lucky or auspicious mark on the body (these are considered to be 32);
 {#dvAtriMSallakzaRopetaH#}; {#lakzaRasaMpannAnnAM gavAmaDaH sasnO#} <ls>K. 64</ls>.
.²6 Any mark or features of the body (indicative of good or bad luck);
 {#kva tadviDastvaM kva ca puRyalakzaRA#} <ls>Ku. 5. 73</ls>; {#kleSAvahA BarturalakzaRAham#} <ls>R. 14. 5</ls>.
.²7 A name, designation, appellation (<ab>oft.</ab> at the end of <ab>comp.</ab>); {#vidiSAlakzaRAM#}
 {#rAjaDAnIm#} <ls>Me. 24</ls>.
.²8 Excellence, merit, good quality; as in {#AhitalakzaRa#} <ls>R. 6. 71</ls> (where
 <ls>Malli.</ls> renders it by {#praKyAtaguRa#} and quotes

 <ls>Ak.</ls>:-- {#guREH pratIte tu kftalakzaRAhitalakzaRO#}).
.²9 An aim, a scope, an object.
.²10 A fixed rate (as of duties); {#nadItIrezu tadvidyAt samudre nAsti#}
 {#lakzaRam#} <ls>Ms. 8. 406</ls>.
.²11 Form, kind, nature.
.²12 Effect, operation.
.²13 Cause, occasion.
.²14 Head, topic, subject.
.²15 Pretence, disguise (= {#lakza#}); {#prasuptalakzaRaH#} <ls>Māl. 7</ls>.
.²16 A line, spot.
.²17 Observation, seeing.
.²18 Indicatory characteristic; {#lakzyate yena tallakzaRam, DUmo lakzaRamagneriti#}
 {#hi vadanti#} <ls>ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 2</ls>.
.²19 A chapter; {#Darmo dvAdaSalakzaRyA vyutpAdyaH#}.
.²20 A sexual organ; {#lakzaRaM lakzaRenEva vadanaM vadanena ca#} <ls>Mb. 13. 40. 58</ls>.

